<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak March M2 +12.8 pct yr/yr vs +13.9pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Slovak March M2 +12.8 pct yr/yr vs +13.9pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The key Slovak money supply aggregate, M2, was 12.8 percent higher, year-on-year, in March 1997, after a year-on-year increase of 13.9 percent in February, the National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Growth in M2 in March 1996 was 24.1 percent.</p>
</text>
